# Tolarian Terror, {6}{U}: "This spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard" (CR 601.2f, 118.7a). On turn 1 Bot1 casts
# Lightning Bolt (an instant) and Duress (a sorcery), so two cards count; the Black Lotus sacrificed on turn 3 is an artifact in the graveyard and counts for
# nothing. On turn 3 Bot1 taps seven mana (Mountain {R}, Mox Jet {B}, Mox Sapphire {U}, Black Lotus {U}{U}{U}, Island {U}) and the Terror costs {4}{U} = five,
# so two blue mana are left in the pool (the reduction of 2, not 1 and not 3). Ward is the second ability and does nothing here.

